ps5-linux-mwifiex: stop a stuck Wi-Fi firmware from freezing all networking

Applies to ps5-linux-mwifiex (tested on 4bce848). install.sh in this guide
applies it automatically; by hand: git apply 0004-mwifiex-txpower-bounded-wait.patch
in the ps5-linux-mwifiex checkout, then run its install.sh.

When the IW620 firmware stops answering (no auth reply after "HostMlme send
auth", then a TXPWR_CFG 0xd1 timeout), woal_set_get_tx_power() waited forever
(MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT) while cfg80211 held the wiphy mutex. NetworkManager holds
RTNL while waiting for that mutex, so every network call on the machine hung
(processes stuck in D state, the desktop froze on anything network related).
The query now uses MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT_TIMEOUT, like the station-info queries in
the existing RTNL bounded-wait patch, so a dead firmware gives a timeout
instead of a freeze.

Adds ps5-iw620-txpower-bounded-wait.patch and the step in install.sh that
applies it after the TX priority patch.

diff --git a/install.sh b/install.sh
index d5c91eb..d1c1612 100755
--- a/install.sh
+++ b/install.sh
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ RTNL_PATCH=$script_dir/ps5-iw620-rtnl-bounded-wait.patch
 HE_PATCH=$script_dir/ps5-iw620-he.patch
 TX_PATCH=$script_dir/ps5-iw620-tx-min128.patch
 PRIORITY_PATCH=$script_dir/ps5-iw620-tx-priority.patch
+TXPWR_PATCH=$script_dir/ps5-iw620-txpower-bounded-wait.patch
 
 MODULE_DIR=/lib/modules/$KERNEL_RELEASE/extra/ps5-iw620
 MODPROBE_CONF=/etc/modprobe.d/ps5-iw620.conf
@@ -181,6 +182,16 @@ prepare_source() {
 	else
 		die "TX priority patch does not apply cleanly in $DRIVER_DIR"
 	fi
+
+	[ -f "$TXPWR_PATCH" ] || die "patch file not found: $TXPWR_PATCH"
+	if git_driver apply --check "$TXPWR_PATCH" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+		say "Applying TX power bounded-wait patch"
+		git_driver apply "$TXPWR_PATCH"
+	elif git_driver apply -R --check "$TXPWR_PATCH" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+		say "TX power bounded-wait patch is already applied"
+	else
+		die "TX power bounded-wait patch does not apply cleanly in $DRIVER_DIR"
+	fi
 }
 
 build_driver() {
diff --git a/ps5-iw620-txpower-bounded-wait.patch b/ps5-iw620-txpower-bounded-wait.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c44245
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ps5-iw620-txpower-bounded-wait.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+--- a/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c
++++ b/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c
+@@ -1904,7 +1904,14 @@
+ 				power_cfg, sizeof(mlan_power_cfg_t),
+ 				sizeof(mlan_power_cfg_t));
+ 
+-	ret = woal_request_ioctl(priv, req, MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT);
++	/* cfg80211 calls this from nl80211_get_interface() and set_tx_power with
++	 * the wiphy mutex held, and NetworkManager can be holding RTNL while it
++	 * waits for that mutex. With MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT a firmware that stops
++	 * answering (TXPWR_CFG 0xd1 timeout) strands wpa_supplicant here forever
++	 * and every network syscall on the machine blocks in D state. Bound it
++	 * like the station-info queries in the RTNL bounded-wait patch.
++	 */
++	ret = woal_request_ioctl(priv, req, MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+ 	if (ret != MLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
+ 		goto done;
+ 
